WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.999
IN and JOIN may appear to answer similar questions
but they have different semantics IN

00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:12.934
asks whether an outer value belongs to a set A join
returns matching

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.607
row combinations If one patient has multiple
admissions the join

00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:24.524
can repeat that patient The IN query keeps the
patient-level outer grain

00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:29.132
Run both queries and compare the outputs carefully
